       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review from here, and 5,100 mg/day is far outside any recognized metformin dosing. I don't know of a standard protocol that supports it. Metformin-associated lactic acidosis can be severe and hard to reverse, so I'd rather not place the order on an unverifiable claim.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Pharmacist verification:** If the protocol exists, the pharmacist who reviewed it can document that in the chart or enter or co-sign the order. Your order system may also have a dose-override or protocol order set for this.\n- **A dose within the labeled range:** I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) right now.\n- **Order note:** If you'd like to attach the protocol name or reference, tell me and I'll include it on a lower-dose order.\n\nShould I enter the 850 mg three-times-daily order, or would you rather take this through pharmacy first?"
